From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:28:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ANGLE at Direct3D feature level 9_3 on Windows 10 Mobile
 (from gecko-w10m)

ANGLE's Direct3D 11 renderer asked for feature level 10_0 and up only, so
on a phone whose GPU stops at 9_3 (Lumia 550, 650, 950) it had no device.
It now also accepts 9_3, last in the list; its clear shaders get their
level 9 forms again (Clear11_FL9.hlsl, compiled offline), without which
every masked or scissored clear failed at 9_3; point sprites, a geometry
shader 9_3 has not got, are not emulated there, and points are one pixel.
These are gecko-w10m's ANGLE changes (its patch 0100, proven on a Lumia
650), its ANGLE_ENABLE_WINDOWS_UWP guards also taking VENETIUM_W10M.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
